@@ -3,3 +3,22 @@
 The Lakeside Windsurf School teaches windsurfing on the lake from April to October, and rents boards and
 sails to its students and to visitors who bring their own experience. This repository holds the software
 of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
+
+## Rental module
+
+`src/index.ts` exports `createRentalService()`, an in-memory service for renting boards and sails.
+
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })` adds an item. `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'`, and `dailyPrice`
+  is the price of one day in integer euro cents.
+- `quote({ itemId, start, end })` returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }` for the period, without reserving it.
+- `book({ itemId, start, end })` reserves the item and returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`.
+
+Periods are ISO-8601 strings at midnight UTC, such as `2026-07-01T00:00:00Z`. `end` is the start of the day
+after the last rented day, so one day is `start: 2026-07-01T00:00:00Z, end: 2026-07-02T00:00:00Z`. Money is
+always an integer number of euro cents. Quoting or booking an unknown item, or a period that is not whole
+days, throws. Booking also throws when the item is already booked for any day of the period.
+
+Periods are half-open, so a booking ending on 3 July does not block one starting on 3 July. Cancellations
+are not implemented yet; the cancellation policy will be added later.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
